I got the times from analyzing the ttyrecs. I wrote a script that
extracts the turncount (if available, some people play without the
"time" option), realtime (if -r is passed to the script), and contents
of all the wishes made in a ttyrec. It's available at
http://sartak.katron.org/nh/ttywish

For the time of entire games, I use jilles' timettyrec, available at
http://www.stack.nl/~jilles/games/ (though indeed ttyrec is an easily-
parseable format, so I've also written my own versions of timettyrec,
but they're in Perl so probably a fair amount slower)

